# `mate` is made in front of both loops and is believed, with its shape, where the closed copy of the loop inside begins; the typed turn that hands over to it has given it a name more. It may be fresh still: what
# arrives is another shape than was believed. The builds of that row are given up as a try is, and every fresh object leaves in front of them; no purchase of the loop around is lost.
# RUN: compile LoopVersioningAttemptsFailed WalkLoopsVersioned mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic LoopVersioningAttemptsFailed 0
# CHECK: statistic WalkLoopsVersioned 7
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# SHELL: number 3 number 6 2 6 {"n":6} {"n":6,"late":2} 3,5,5
